      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The autotaxin-lysophophatidic acid (ATX-LPA) signaling pathway is implicated in a variety of human disease states including angiogenesis, autoimmune diseases, cancer, fibrotic diseases, inflammation, neurodegeneration, and neuropathic pain, among others. As a result, ATX-LPA has become of significant interest within both the industrial and the academic communities. This review aims to provide a concise overview of the development of novel ATX inhibitors, including the disclosure of the first ATX clinical trial data."},
